2026-08-09T08:47:01.4980249Z [36;1m# Do NOT export UserNM here, however tempting the `UserNM=true` trick[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4980819Z [36;1m# from AGENTS.md looks. It is a development shortcut, not a CI setting.[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4981190Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4981385Z [36;1m# R takes the nm program from $UserNM in[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4981763Z [36;1m# tools:::read_symbols_from_object_file, and that function serves two[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4982216Z [36;1m# callers, not one: building `symbols.rds` at install time (which[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4982608Z [36;1m# src/Makevars puts on the `all:` target), *and*[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4983008Z [36;1m# tools:::check_so_symbols scanning the built .so during `R CMD check`.[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4983469Z [36;1m# Pointing nm at `true` blinds the second one, so the check finds no[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4983918Z [36;1m# symbols at all and reports "Found no calls to 'R_registerRoutines',[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4984381Z [36;1m# 'R_useDynamicSymbols'" -- a NOTE, and with error_on = "note" a failed[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4984840Z [36;1m# check on a package that registers its routines perfectly well.[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4985165Z [36;1m#[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4985440Z [36;1m# It is not worth scoping to the installs either: measured, the sweep is[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4985883Z [36;1m# ~0.25 s per 90 MB of unstripped objects, so ~10-20 s for the whole[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4986307Z [36;1m# ~2.5 GB tree -- under 5% of a commit's floor, against a footgun that[0m
2026-08-09T08:47:01.4986659Z [36;1m# silently weakens a CRAN check.[0m
